## abm-video-bgdt project (overrides the notes above)

This project is built with the abm-video-bgdt pipeline. Run `node tools/bin/abm-video.mjs next` and do exactly what it prints.
- It prints NEXT (the task), RUN (the command) and WHY. Run it, then ask `next` again. Never invent a step.
- You write only: the facts (`capture/extracted/visible-text.txt`), the script (`script.src.txt`, see the skill's
  references/script-authoring.md), `scenes.json` (references/direction.md) and the user's gate answers.
- Making the whole video alone: follow the skill's references/autonomous-run.md step by step.
- Gates 1 and 4: show the user the file `next` names, then record their own words with `abm-video gate <n> --approve "…"`
  or `--reject "…"`. Gates 2 and 3 of a directed lesson: approve them yourself with `--approve --by agent "…"`, only
  after `abm-video gate <n> --check` shows every check ✓.
- Never edit the skill's files or `tools/`, and never loosen a threshold in `video.config.json`: report the problem instead.
- Never edit `index.html` or a compiled frame's HTML; change `scenes.json` and run `abm-video run compile`.
- The HyperFrames CLI stays pinned at `hyperframes@{{PIN}}`: never run `upgrade`, `skills update` or `add` here.
- Narration comes from the VieNeu-TTS API (`abm-video run tts`) and captions from `tools/build-karaoke.mjs`; do not use
  faceless-explainer's own TTS or captions.
- Machine problems: `node tools/bin/abm-video.mjs doctor --fix`.
